# Lockfiles
**/*.lock
**/*-lock.json
**/*-lock.yaml
**/*-lock.yml

# Generated files and build products
**/generated/**
**/*.generated.*
**/dist/**
**/build/**
**/coverage/**
packages/engine/assets/**
packages/frontend/src/i18n/locales/**
packages/frontend/src/game/screens/hud/spellbook-seed.json
packages/inventory/types/**
packages/party/types/**
packages/sdk/types/**
packages/sdk/src/deployment/release.json
packages/move/scripts/out/**
test/gold/.build/**
test/gold/out/**

# Test source is exempt so RED-FIRST bug proofs do not pay production-code rent.
# `**` (not `*`) on purpose: test roots are not all one level deep, and not all singular. The
# singular-and-shallow pattern silently charged rent to whole test trees — packages/rpc/indexer/tests/
# and every packages/move/*/tests/ suite (128 Move test files) — which is how train-25 booked a
# 537-line Rust integration test as production debt.
packages/**/test/**
packages/**/tests/**
test/**
# Rust keeps its test modules beside the source it tests, so the exemption is a filename class there.
# The Move suffix twin (*_tests.move) needs no rule: all 128 already live under a tests/ dir above.
**/*_tests.rs
**/tests.rs

# Fixtures and captured evidence
**/fixtures/**
**/*.fixture.*
**/*.snap

# Test files — RED-FIRST manufactures test mass by design; it is the payment, not the debt (#1713)
**/*.test.*
**/*.spec.*
